# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 1 — CONTROL Q2: does ordered CHOICE give back?
#
# The one-difference partner of Q1: same "a successful sub-match starves the element after
# it" shape, but the sub-match comes from a CHOICE instead of a quantifier. On input "abc"
# the alternative `"a"` succeeds and then `"c"` fails at `b`.
#   - a committing choice   -> REJECT
#   - a giving-back choice  -> retries `"ab"`, then `"c"` matches -> ACCEPT
#
# REQUIRED VERDICT: ACCEPT.
#
# ⭐ Q1 vs Q2 is the whole finding: the SAME engine gives back at a choice and refuses to
# give back at a quantifier. `.17`'s blocker is that asymmetry, not "PEG does not backtrack".
@entry: true
scratch := ( "a" | "ab" ) "c"
